# State Management

Use **Cubit + flutter_bloc** by default. Use **Bloc** only when events, transformers, or many event types add real clarity. Do not add another state-management package.

## Cubit/Bloc

Handle business logic, I/O via injected services, async coordination, and loading/success/empty/error. Prevent duplicate in-flight loads when needed. Never emit after `close()`.

Prefer constructor injection:

```dart
class HomeCubit extends Cubit<HomeState> {
  HomeCubit(this._userService) : super(const HomeState.initial());
  final UserService _userService;
}
```

Do not new up services inside Cubits when they can be injected. Pages must not call APIs or databases.

## State

Immutable state (Equatable as used in this project). Include only data the UI needs. Use Initial/Loading/Success/Empty/Error when relevant — no extra states.

Keep **local UI state** in the widget: controllers, focus, expansion, animations, ephemeral visuals.

## Bloc widgets

- `BlocBuilder` for rebuilds
- `BlocListener` for navigation, snackbars, dialogs
- `BlocConsumer` only when both are required in one place

Use `buildWhen`/`listenWhen` to cut noise. Keep rebuild scopes small.
